# meryl/ — binary k-mer database (not committed)
#
# Merqury's truth k-mer database lives here in real cluster runs as a
# directory of binary index files (~10 GB for catfish at k=21). Too
# large + too binary for git; rebuild via the cluster pipeline:
#
#   meryl count k=21 \
#     output truth.k21.meryl \
#     /scratch/reads/fClaHyb_dam.illumina.fq.gz \
#     /scratch/reads/fClaHyb_sire.illumina.fq.gz \
#     /scratch/reads/fClaHyb_dam.hifi.fq.gz \
#     /scratch/reads/fClaHyb_sire.hifi.fq.gz
#
# This .gitkeep is what holds the empty directory in git so the
# expected path exists for tooling that resolves `merqury/meryl/`.
